    "rail": {
      "_note": "One row of slots, because 90 units of drawer is one row. `pad` is measured from the silhouette edge; `slot` is the drawn cell, `slotTop` where it is drawn and `pitch` its stride. `label` is the vertical bucket caption that divides the rail into groups. At 1672 canvas width the rail shows about 19 cells, so a bag of twenty to thirty items is one or two swipes.",
      "pad": 26,
      "top": 734,
      "height": 88,
      "_box": "The scroll box is 88 tall while the row it holds is 66, and the slots are centred in it. The 11 units of slack above and below are hit area: a 66-unit cell is 66 real px on a desktop but 33 on a phone held sideways, under the ~44 floor, and the ::after trick base.css uses cannot expand past the scroll box because overflow-y is hidden. 11 is exactly (44 / 0.5 - 66) / 2, the expansion needed at the landscape layout's worst case k.",
